{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/1411183-scarn-s-magic-origin","id":1411183,"title":"Scarn's magic origin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-31T03:48:50-07:00","id":1411183,"title":"Scarn's magic origin","content":"Hi,<br /> <br /> I played some years age as a player in scarred land's settings, but I would like to use this setting to play with &quot;Chroniques oubli\u00e9s&quot;, a french alternative version from the 3rd OGL. I read actually the player's guide to scarred land for the 5th ed. Pretty complete for a first book (and I like the new spirit of this edition) , but I canno't find from where magic in scarred land come from. Mesos is the sire of sorcery but it seems that he invent a way to master arcane magic, but the magic itself doesn't come from Him. So basically magic is some sentence which give a form to the arcarne energy if I well understood. But what is this energy ?<br /> <br /> PS :I'm not an usual D&amp;D player so that could explain my confusion. I only played in Scarred Land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26401-fariss","name":"Fariss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T05:14:18-07:00","id":1411193,"title":"","content":"3e's Player's Guide to Wizards, Bards and Sorcerers mentions two different theories on the origins of magic - one, that it's always been a part of the universe, or two, that it began with the titans.<br /> <br /> So you could make the case that arcane energy is a fundamental component of Scarn's cosmos.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T05:46:31-07:00","id":1411199,"title":"","content":"A clear answer, thanks to you, I will take a look at the player's guide to Wizards, didn't think it could contain some background...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26401-fariss","name":"Fariss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-31T12:05:51-07:00","id":1411234,"title":"","content":"Word of warning: it's a tiny little bit in the first page of the first Wizards chapter.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough, chapter 4, one of the Bard chapters, has a theory that could also be appropriated for this, amongst the various theories on bardic magic they offer: the primal sound philosophy, which holds that all of creation was brought about by a single sound or word that reflects every existing thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:13:55-07:00","id":1411790,"title":"","content":"The PG's were the best for that sort of theory-crafting. There seemed to be a low-key theme of &quot;arcane magic is the natural magic of the world&quot; through Mesos. But that theory had its flaws, which was nice of the writers, and gave us a whole host of other magical theories.<br /> <br /> Contrasted with the Slarecians where their powers were utterly alien and did not belong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13194-psyclus","name":"Psyclus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T13:50:49-07:00","id":1416336,"title":"","content":"As someone who uses Vampiric Aura a lot and loves to give lifelink to creatures with my Lurkers, Tainted Remedy would be horrible for me to play against - I often take damage in early turns, and recoup it vampiric life drain in mid-late game. Vampiric Aura on a semi-powerful creature when opponent is mostly non-flier is usually a win condition - even if they have stuff like drones to block me with, every block is healing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26355-wagonicfolding","name":"wagonicfolding","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-05T05:30:56-08:00","id":1438110,"title":"","content":"Last time i played on Scarn was about the time the Guide to the Pathfinder version came out.<br /> With a funny dude of a wandering swashbuckling necromancer-merchant-diplomat from Hollowfaust.<br /> All too many of my Scarred Lands PCs have been surprisingly cheery and energetic types hailing from that city it seems. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looks like i have some serious catching up to do one those days, considering i haven't even caught up with 5e D&amp;D yet.<br /> <br /> More in line with the thread's topic (i hope), a major incidental plot element of our campaign ended up being the god of Scarn's 2nd moon, fallen brother of Belsameth &amp; Madriel, or to be more precise, a number of relics, objects of power and mostly forgotten ruins or abandoned places touched by remnants of its particular brand of divine magic or that of a few of its surviving servants &amp;/or worshippers, leading to much exploration, discoveries - and troubles, obviously.<br /> <br /> (Also a bunch of homebrewing using materials from Occult Adventures, mixed with some elements from Ravenloft &amp; Spelljammer)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-05-2021, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}